  // %arg1: conv_transpose.bias, shape [7]
  // %arg2: input, shape [batch=16, in_channels=6, 6,6,6]

  // Step 1: conv_transpose (3D transposed convolution)
  // conv_transpose in PyTorch is a transposed convolution.
  // StableHLO convolution can do transposed conv by setting lhs_dilation > 1 and reversing kernel spatial dims.
  // Input shape: [16,6,6,6,6] (NCDHW)
  // Weight shape: [6,7,5,5,5] (in_channels, out_channels, kD,kH,kW)
  // PyTorch conv_transpose weight shape is (in_channels, out_channels, kD,kH,kW)
  // StableHLO convolution expects kernel shape [output_feature, input_feature, spatial...]
  // So we must transpose %arg0 from [6,7,5,5,5] to [7,6,5,5,5] to match OIHW layout.
  // Also, for transposed conv, lhs_dilation = stride (2,2,2), rhs_dilation=1, padding=kernel_size - 1 - padding = 5-1-2=2
  // dimension_numbers: input [b,f,0,1,2], kernel [o,i,0,1,2], output [b,f,0,1,2]

